find your passion  successful businesses are built around  entrepreneurs who are intensely  passionate about what they're doing  and they build the business up around it  if you do not follow your passion if  you're just trying to be successful  you're just trying to make money it's  never going to happen you will not have  success  you're going to go after failure after  failure after failure trying to jump on  the next quick money-making opportunity  and it's never going to work out because  you are not passionate about the product  or service that you're selling it's  critical it's everything it's the number  one rule in business  no strategy can save you if you're not  passionate about what you're selling  i got a question from a reader  uh ann keat who wrote in the same  he wants to start a business and so he  wanted my advice and and i wrote back to  say hey ankit what are you passionate  about and he said my passion is i want  to be successful  i want to have success that's not enough  that's not a true passion  and key you have to do something  that has the potential to change the  world you have to believe  so  firmly in what you're doing and that  it's the right thing to do  if you look at any successful famous  entrepreneur you look at how they got  started  it was not to make a ton of money  although that's a byproduct i'm not  saying start a charity i want you to  make a ton of money i want you to have a  ton of success  but it starts  with having a deep passion for something  it starts with you seeing a problem in  the world and wanting to change it  wanting to make it better  and everything flows from that  and you can share your passion you can  share your story and the people who will  buy from the people who will work for  you the people who will cover you in  media or investors they're going to come  because they believe in your passion  they believe in your vision  i believe in entrepreneurs i love  helping entrepreneurs it's my passion i  would 